---
number: 635
title: Lead Them, My God to Thee
author: Robert W. Lowry, 1868 Adapt. by F. E. Belden
composer: F. E. Belden
sp_category: "40"
topic: Children
---

[verse 1]
Lead them, my God to Thee,
Lead them to Thee,
These children dear of mine,
Thou givest me;
O, by Thy love divine,
Lead them, my God, to Thee;
Lead them, my God, to Thee,
Lead them to Thee.

[verse 2]
When earth looks bright and fair,
Festive and gay,
Let no delusive snare
Lure them astray;
But from temptation’s power,
Lead them, my God, to Thee;
Lead them, my God, to Thee,
Lead them to Thee.

[verse 3]
E’en for such little ones,
Christ came a child,
And in this world of sin
Lived undefiled.
O, for His sake, I pray,
Lead them, my God, to Thee;
Lead them, my God, to Thee,
Lead them to Thee.

[verse 4]
Yea, though my faith be dim,
I would believe
That Thou this precious gift
Wilt now receive;
O, take their young hearts now,
Lead them, my God, to Thee;
Lead them, my God, to Thee,
Lead them to Thee.
